{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>For [you have made]</b> etc. The sense: many cities will be destroyed when Gog and Magog come, and in the words of R. Moses the Priest, regarding the days of Sennacherib:" "<b>For a heap.</b> Like unto this heap (Genesis 31:51):" "<b>Strangers' palace.</b> They are the exiled nations." "<b>From a city.</b> From any city."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:04.798994515Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}